Created `tests/repair.test.ts` covering all three behaviors of `repairBuilding`:

- **No-op when settlement lacks the building** — two cases: a settlement that has a *different* building (`hut`) and one with none at all. Both assert the returned object is the identical reference (`toBe`) and that resources/buildings are untouched.
- **Half cost, rounded up per resource** — the storehouse case (odd wood cost `ceil(25/2)=13`, even stone `ceil(10/2)=5`) and a farm case where *both* resources are odd (`ceil(15/2)=8`, `ceil(5/2)=3`), verifying each resource rounds up independently.
- **Never below zero** — a storehouse repair needing 13 wood against only 10 available clamps wood to `0` while stone still deducts normally.

